    "question": "Sofia and her mother go to the grocery store and buys 10kgs of oranges to be used in their home for the week. While at the store, Sofia's father calls and says they're to add 5 more kgs since their neighbor also wanted some supplies. When they reach home, they estimated that for the next coming two weeks they'll have to buy twice as many oranges each week for the supplies to be enough. What the total quantity of oranges they would have bought after the three weeks.",
    "gold": "75",
    "answer": "For the first week, they bought 10 + 5 = <<10+5=15>>15kgs.\nFor the next week, they bought twice the quantity of oranges which is 2*15 = <<2*15=30>>30kgs.\nFor the next two weeks, the total quantity of oranges bought is 30*2 = <<30*2=60>>60 kgs.\nThe total quantity for the three weeks is 60+15=<<60+15=75>>75 kgs\n#### 75"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total quantity of oranges Sofia and her family will have bought after three weeks, we need to break down the problem step by step.\n\n1. **Initial Purchase:**\n   Sofia and her mother initially bought 10 kg of oranges.\n\n2. **Additional Purchase:**\n   Sofia's father called and said they need to add 5 more kg of oranges. So, the total quantity of oranges bought so far is:\n   \\[\n   10 \\text{ kg} + 5 \\text{ kg} = 15 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Next Two Weeks:**\n   For the next two weeks, they need to buy twice as many oranges each week as they did in the first week. Since they bought 15 kg in the first week, in the second week they will buy:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 15 \\text{ kg} = 30 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n   And in the third week, they will buy:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 15 \\text{ kg} = 30 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n   So, the total quantity of oranges bought in the next two weeks is:\n   \\[\n   30 \\text{ kg} + 30 \\text{ kg} = 60 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Total Quantity After Three Weeks:**\n   Adding the quantities from the first week and the next two weeks, the total quantity of oranges bought after three weeks is:\n   \\[\n   15 \\text{ kg} + 60 \\text{ kg} = 75 \\text{ kg}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total quantity of oranges they would have bought after the three weeks is \\(\\boxed{75}\\).",
